\pard\keep\keepn\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 84\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -133\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Ps.-Lucius Annaeus Seneca}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Hercules furens, tragoedia cum glossis}}
\par \pard\keep\keepn\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (84\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Federproben, darunter: Ovidius, Tristia, lib. 3,III,17: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Te loquor absentem, te vox mea nominat vnam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (84\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Argumentum: \u8250 \'9b{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Argumentum huius tragedie\u8249 \'8b est, quod Hercules, filius Jouis, natus ex Ackhmena}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  vxore Amphitrionis, habuit vxorem Megeram nomine, filiam Creontis regis Thebaanii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 nobilissimam et prestantissimam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Illa tragedia habet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quinque actus et quelibet debet habere vt Oracius in arte\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [poetica]: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nec quinto fuit productior actu\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (V. 189). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Primus actus continet querelam Junonis contra Jouem eius maritum, quia non uult laborare in nocturno labore\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Inuentor primus tragediarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 fuit Esculus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Aischylos) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Grecus, deinde Sofoclos, postea Eurapides \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (!). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Sed apud Latinos primus fuit Seneca tragicus, vnde Oracius in arte\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [poetica]: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Post hunc persone paleeque repertor Esculus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (V. 278f.) \u8230 \'85 \endash  (85\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -133\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Lucii Aney Senece Cordubensis Hercules furens tragedia prima foeliciter incipit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . [Iuno]: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Soror tonantis (hoc enim solum michi | Nomen relictum est) semper alienum Iouem}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  | \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Ac templa summi vidua diserui etheris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 The\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [seus]: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nostra te tellus manet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  | \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Illic solutam cede gradiuus manum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  | \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Restituit armis: illa te, Alcide, vocat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  | \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Facere innocentes terra que superos solet. Finis adest\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (85\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Marginalglossen: \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Cristo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, vielm. Callisto) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Liconis regis Archadie filia comes Diane dee in venationem. Illa Cristo propter eius pulchritudinem amata fuit a Joue\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  134\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -135\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Druck: L. Annaei Senecae tragoediae, recognovit brevique adnotatione critica instruxit Otto \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Zwierlein\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Reprint, with corrections. Oxford 1991 (Scriptorum classicorum bibliotheca Oxoniensis), S. 3-50. Seneca, Hercules furens. Einleitung, Text, \u220 \'dcbersetzung und Kommentar von Margarethe \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Billerbeck\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Leiden u.a. 1999 (Mnemosyne 187), S. 94-178. \endash  Lit.: Alexander P. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Mac Gregor\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , The manuscripts of Seneca's tragedies. A handlist, in: Aufstieg und Niedergang der r\u246 \'f6mischen Welt (ANRW). Geschichte und Kultur Roms im Spiegel der neueren Forschung 2,32,2: Sprache und Literatur (Literatur der Julisch-Claudischen und der Flavischen Zeit), hrsg. von Hildegard \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Temporini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  / Wolfgang \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Haase\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Berlin u.a. 1985, S. 1135-1241, hier S. 1151 Nr. T 107 (diese Hs.).}

