\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 Erl\u228 \'e4uterung zum hebr\u228 \'e4ischen Alphabet: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Non statim vbicumque ex}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [A littera, que] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 apud Hebreos dicitur aleph, ponuntur nomina\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , [estimandum est, ipsam solam esse, que ponitur] \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 nobis videantur in interpretatione variare\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Hieronymus, De nominibus Hebraicis veteris testamenti, lib.1, ed. PL 23, 773A-774A). \endash  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Quod de A diximus, hoc ipsum quoque in B littera obseruandum est}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quibus quasi literis et exordiis in dei doctrina tenera adhuc et lactens viri iusti eruditur infancia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Stegm\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 ller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , RB 9906). \endash  Hebr\u228 \'e4isches und griechisches Alphabet sowie Kardinalzahlen:\plain \f2\lang1037\fs24 \u1488 \'e0 \plain \f3\i\lang1032\fs24  Aleph doctrina, \u913 \'c1 Alpha, I Mia; \plain \f2\lang1037\fs24 \u1489 \'e1\plain \f3\i\lang1032\fs24  Beth domus, \u914 \'c2 Beda, II Dia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85\plain \f2\lang1037\fs24 \u1514 \'fa \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Thau signa\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f3\i\lang1032\fs24 \u969 \'f9 o longa, Ogdacusin dccc; \u8593 ^ Ennacose, Niacusin dcccc; M mille, Chile \plain \f4\i\fs24 \u298 \'ce\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Frankfurt, StuUB, {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5007[0].501m/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Ms. Barth. 113}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , 97\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va-c\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ).}

