\pard\keep\keepn\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 220\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -292\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Johannes de Segovia}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Explanatio de tribus veritatibus fidei}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx1560\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Incipit explanacio de tribus veritatibus fidei decretatis per sacram generalem Sinodum Basiliensem. Item et de quinque conclusionibus, ex quibus Eugenius quondam papa iiii\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 us\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  arguitur hereticus, iterum in reuocatos errores prolapsus, facta per dominum cardinalem sancti Calixti videlicet de Segobia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Magnus predicator veritatis Paulus apostolus, Doctor gencium, in vniuerso mundo virtutem fidei}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  illibatam custodire debere omnes docens fideles\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et quomodo constat de eius pertinacia, ita ut potuerit legitime condempnari sinodali iudicio tamquam hereticus etc. Jo[hannes] Heller.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Lit.: Concilium Basiliense 1\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 ,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  S. 28-30\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 ; Fromherz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Johannes von Segovia, S. 152 Nr. 7 (Hs. genannt); \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Hern\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 \u225 \'e1\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 ndez Montes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Obras, S. 293f. Nr. 32 (Hs. genannt); \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Kr\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 \u228 \'e4\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 mer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Konsens, S. 134 Anm. 22 (Hs. genannt), 244-246, 444; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Santiago-Otero\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Manuscritos, S. 105 (Hs. genannt), 116f.; Jesse Dayton \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Mann\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , The historian and the truths. Juan de Segovia's Explanatio de tribus veritatibus fidei. Chicago, Univ., Diss. 1993 (nicht eingesehen). \endash  Zur Rezeption Wilhelms von Ockham vgl. Jesse Dayton \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Mann\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , William of Ockham, Juan de Segovia, and Heretical Pertinacity, in: Mediaeval Studies 56 (1994), S. 67-88, hier S. 77 Anm. 49, S. 80f. Anm. 63, S. 88 (mit Zitaten aus vorliegender Hs.).}

