\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Egidius decanus Cameracensis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . \endash  \u8250 \'9b{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 A\u8249 \'8bVdistis, Reuerendissimi patres, Illustrissime princeps, celeberrimi, incliti et doctissimi viri}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1  venerabilesque oratores famosi Regni Bohemie, profundam, precelsam et veram posicionem de communione diuinissime Ewkaristie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ut fulgeant iusti et tamquam scintille in arundineto discurrent\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (Sap. 3,7), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 quod nobis prestet in commune, in cuius nomine congregati sumus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \endash  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0]/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 Kolophon}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Explicit Responsio ad secundum articulum Bohemorum, edita per magistrum Egidium decanum Cameracensem in Concilio Basiliensi super peccata publica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (13.-17. Februar 1433).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Druck: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Mansi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  29, Sp. 868-972. \endash  Lit.: Victorinus \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Doucet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Magister Aegidius Carlerii (\u8224 \'86 1472) eiusque quaestio de immaculata conceptione B. Mariae Virginis, in: Antonianum 5 (1930), S. 405-442, hier S. 415 Nr. 3 (ohne diese Hs.); \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Vooght\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  (s. 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ), S. 125-137; Thomas \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Sullivan\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Parisian licentiates in theology a.D. 1373-1500. A biographical register 2. Leiden u.a. 2011 (Education and society in the Middle Ages and Renaissance 37), S. 134-137.}

