\pard\keep\keepn\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -59\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Antonius Luschus}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Commentarium in orationes Ciceronis}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx12825\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 In Christi nomine eius quam virginis matris gloriose Marie Amen. Antonii Lusci Vincentini secretarii illustrissimi ducis Mediolani ad suum fratrem optimum atque carissimum Ascolfinum de Marmonibus secretarii magniffici\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Francisci de Barbauariis inquisitio artis in orationibus Ciceronis incipit. Prohemium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Prolog: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Magna res est eloquentia, frater insignis atque optime}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 , maiorque profecto\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  (6\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Oratio de imperio Cn. Pompei: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Argumentum oracionis Pompeianae\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Cicero creatus pretor Romanus duo persuadere nititur populo Romano}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 autoritate fide constancia etc. articulus. Explicit Pompeiana\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash \plain \f1\lang1033\fs18\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (17\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 )\plain \f1\lang1033\fs18\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 Pro Milone: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Argumentum orationis Miloniane\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Titus Aninus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Milo, ciuis Romanus, sibi infestissimum et inimicissimum Romanum ciuem P. Clodium habuit \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 vestram virtutem iusticiam fidem etc. articulus est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Explicit Miloniania feliciter\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b. \endash  (40\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Pro Marcello: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Argumentum oracionis de laudibus Cesaris occasione M. Marcelli per Cesarem restituti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Marcellus ciuis Romanus amplissimus atque clarissimus in dissensione ciuili\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 magnis curis molestiis doloribus etc. articulus est. Explicit de laudibus Cesaris propter M. Marcellum\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs18\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 restitutum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (43\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Pro Ligario: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Argumentum oracionis pro Q. Ligario\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Qvintus Ligarius ciuis Romanus cum C. Considio consule profectus est legatus in Affricam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  propria fecit hominis ut Quintilianus ait. Explicit pro Q. Ligario\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (51\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Pro Deiotaro \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Argumentum oracionis pro rege Deyotharo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Deiotharous\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 rex amicissimus p\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [opulo] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [omano] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 bello ciuili cum Pompeio fuit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 memoriam tuam implorat etc. dissolutum est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Explicit pro rege Deyotharo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b. \endash  (56\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Pro Archia: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Argumentum oracionis pro A\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [ulo] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Licinio archia poeta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Avlus Licinius archias poeta Anthiochie natus Rome uixit in amicitia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 qui par res gestas etc. repeticio est. Deo gratias Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Explicit pro A\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [ulo] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Licinio archia poeta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b. \endash  60\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -67\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx12825\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx12825\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Es werden sechs von insgesamt elf kommentierten Reden \u252 \'fcberliefert; m\u246 \'f6glicherweise waren 60\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 -67\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  f\u252 \'fcr die restlichen Kommentare vorgesehen. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Bertalot\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , IHL 2,1 Nr. 2179, 11364 (Hs. genannt). \endash  Druck: GW 2739-2740 = BSB-Ink A-791-792. \endash  Zu Luschus s. Rep. Fontium 7 (1997), S. 346f. (mit weiterer Lit.).}

