\pard\keep\keepn\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -152\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Adnotationes in quinque libros Decretalium. Libri I-III}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa60\itap0 X 1.1: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 De summa trinitate et fide katholica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . [{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 F]irmiter credimus (X 1.1.1). Nota summa ponitur, quod vnusquisque fidelis secundum rationem}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  fidem katholicam debet credere et simpliciter confiteri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Decr. cum glossis, Sp. 7 Z. 35f.). \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Dampnamus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (X 1.1.2). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Licet quis erret in fide, non debet hereticus iudicari, dum tamen fidem romane ecclesie suscipere sit paratus vel eam se tenere fateatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Jo. An., Bl. a vi\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). \endash  X 1.2: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 De constitucionibus. Canonum statuta custodiantur ab omnibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (X 1.2.1). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Constituciones canonum ab omnibus sunt seruande\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Jo. An., Bl. a vii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nota constitucio est ius humanum et est duplex: Aliud in scriptis redactum, quod proprie dicitur constitucio. Aliud solo vsu vtencium approbatum, quod dicitur consuetudo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Bern. Pap. ad X 1.1.\u167 \'a7 1). \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Cognoscentes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (X 1.2.2). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Constitucio respicit futura, non preterita\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Jo. An., Bl. a viii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 nota sex casus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , [in quibus] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 punitur aliquis non tamen sine causa. W\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [ersus]: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Paupertas, odium, vicium, fauor, scelus, ordo, hiis quis punitur sine culpa et non sine causa personas spoliant et loca iure suo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Decr. cum glossis, Sp. 15f., Glosse zu h). \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Translato sacerdocio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (X 1.2.3). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quod de vno connexorum constituitur, ad alterum connexum ostenditur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Jo. An., Bl. a viii\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 W\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [ersus]: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quia vere est eadem ratio, ibi est idem ius et de similibus idem est iudicium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ; es folgen cc. 4-13; (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) X 1.3.1-4, 6, 5 ,7-43; (9\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) X 1.4.1-11; (12\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) X 1.5.1-6; 14\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer; (14\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Illud notabile pertinet ad capitulum sequens De electione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , [c.] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Cum in cunctis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (X 1.6.7): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Iterum quis compellitur ad ordines per subtraccionem beneficii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 nisi alias valor\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, vielm. valde) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 vtilis et necessarius esset huic ecclesie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (VI 1.6.14, vgl. Lib. Sextus cum suis glossis, Sp. 107, Glosse zu g); (15\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) X 1.6.1-36.11. \endash  Schaltzettel: (42\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quid sit procurator. Procurator is est, qui negocia aliena mandato sibi a domino facto gerenda gratuiuto suscepit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 sed quia gerendum suscepit vt ff. Man\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [dati vel contra], \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 l.\plain \f1\b\i\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Si remunerandi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (D. 17.1.6) (Sum. aurea ad X 1.38 \u167 \'a7 1); (42\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 )\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Sunt quedam persone, que in propriis personis non admittuntur ad agendum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quorum singula singulos sindicos habere debent, vt 9 q. iii Cum simus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (C.9 q.3 c.3) (Sum. aurea ad X 1.38 \u167 \'a7 5). \endash  (43\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) X 1.37.1-43.14.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (47\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) X 2: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Sequitur liber secundus de Iudiciis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . Rest der Seite sowie 48\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer. \endash  (48\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) X 2.1.1-24.36. \endash  Schaltzettel: (78\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nota quatuordecim casus, in quibusdam pater potest filium exhereditare. Primus casus siue prima causa est, si filius violentas manus iniecit in parentes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quatuordecima\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [causa], \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 si pater sit katholicus, filius vero hereticus. W\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [ersus]: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Bis septem}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17  [ex] {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 causis filius potest exhereditari}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 . Parentes feriat vel verbum si graue dicat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 (vgl. Charles \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Cahier\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Quelque six mille proverbes et aphorismes usuels emprunt\u233 \'e9s \u224 \'e0 notre \u226 \'e2ge et aux si\u232 \'e8cles derniers. Paris 1856, S. 529 Nr. 1403). \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nota septem sunt cause, propter quas pater potest exhereditari a filio. Prima si pater accusauit filium de crimine capitali uel accu\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [sauit] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 eum de crimine lese maiestatis uel heresis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 octaua superadditur, si filius sit katholicus et pater hereticus. W\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [ersus]: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Sed pater ex octo filii conspuerat honorem}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Accusat filium veneno, si potat illum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85 \endash  (78\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nota frater exhereditari a fratre tribus causis: Nam non potest frater rumpere testamentum fratris uel sororis nec instituisset turpem personam, in Auth\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [enticis], \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 De nup\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [tiis], \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 \u167 \'a7 Testamentum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!, vielm. Ingratitudinem), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 coll\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [atio] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 iiii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Nov. 22.46.4). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Prima causa si procurauit mortem fratris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 tertia si sue substancie procurat iacturam et sic porcio eius ad patrem et ad alios fratres perueniet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Nota condiciones, que subintelliguntur in iuramentis: Prima ut hec, si placet pape, ut supra eodem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [c.] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Venientes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (X 2.24.19). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Iterum hec, si placuit deo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 et hec verba sunt in compromissariis iuramentis, sed in assertoriis nulla condicio subintelligitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (80\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) X 2.25.1-30.9. \endash  (95\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) X 3.1.1-50.10; (152\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Et sic est finis libri tertii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Kompilation aus verschiedenen Kommentaren zu den Dekretalen, nach stichprobenartiger Pr\u252 \'fcfung zu Beginn von Buch 1 wohl mit Schwerpunkt auf den Novellen des Johannes Andreae. \endash  Siglen (in alphabetischer Reihenfolge): Bern. Pap. = Bernardi Papiensis \u8230 \'85 Summa decretalium, ed. Ernst Adolph Theodor \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Laspeyres\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Regensburg 1860. \endash  Decr. cum glossis = Decretales D. Gregorii Papae IX. suae integritati una cum glossis restitutae. Lyon 1584. \endash  Jo. An. = Johannes Andreae, Novella super quinque libris Decretalium (GW 1729; BSB-Ink I-319). \endash  Lib. Sextus cum suis glossis = Liber Sextus decretalium D. Bonifacii Papae VIII. Clementis Papae V. Constitutiones. Extravagantes tum viginti D. Ioannis Papae XXII. tum communes. Haec omnia cum suis glossis suae integritati restituta. Lyon 1584. \endash  Sum. aurea = Henrici de Segusio Cardinalis Hostiensis Summa aurea. Ad vetustissimos codices summa fide diligentiaque nunc denuo collata \u8230 \'85 Lyon 1597}

