\pard\keep\keepn\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 142\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -229\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Marcus Tullius Cicero}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 De officiis libri III, cum glossis}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Quamquam te, Marce fili, annum iam audientem Cratippum}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  idque Athenis habundare oportet preceptis institutisque philosophie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 si talibus monimentis preceptisque letabere. Expliciunt feliciter libri officiorum Marci Tulii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Augustinus: Excellunt cunctos hii libros philosophorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Initia Nr. 6039; \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Walther\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Proverbia Nr. 8380c).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Druck: M. Tulli Ciceronis De officiis, recognovit brevique adnotatione critica instruxit Michael \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Winterbottom\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Oxford 1994 (Scriptorum classicorum bibliotheca Oxoniensis), S. 1-161. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Ders\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ., The Transmission of Cicero's De Officiis, in: The Classical Quarterly, New Series 43 (1993), S. 215-242, bes. S. 234-242 mit \u220 \'dcberblick \u252 \'fcber die hsl. \u220 \'dcberlieferung nach 1200, ebd. S. 239 (Hs. genannt).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (142\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Marginalglossen: \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Omnes Marci Tulii Ciceronis simplicis honestatis. Quattuor sunt partes prudencia, scilicet iusticia, fortitudo, temperancia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 modestia est, per quam pudor honestus curam et stabilem comparat autoritatem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Cicero, De inventione II, 159-163). \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quoniam in principio cuiuslibet autoris quattuor sunt inquirenda: Intencio videlicet est, cui parte philosophie supponitur et que materia, vtilitas percipiatur et titulus. Intencio Tulii in hoc opere est edocere filium suum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85}

