\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 Utrum homo possit resurgere a peccato mortali sine auxilio gratie}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1  gratum facientis. Arguitur quod sic: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Illud quod preexigitur ad gratiam, fit sine gratia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 reparari non potest sine exteriori auxilio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . Thomas de Aquino, Sum. theol. Ia-I\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ae\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , q. 109, art. 7. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \endash  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 Utrum bonum opus, additum operi, reddat operantem dignum maiori premio}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  [essentiali]\u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 sed opera propter operantem acceptat et remunerat et ideo non est simile etc\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . Bonaventura, IV Sent., lib. 2, dist. 40, art. 2, q. 3, in: \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 S. Bonaventurae Opera omnia. Iussu et auctoritate reverendissimi P. Bernardini a Portu Romatino ... edita studio et cura pp. Collegii a S. Bonaventura \u8230 \'85 Bd. 2. Quaracchi 1885, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 S. 931-933. \endash  (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 Utrum peccati dimissa redeant quoad reatum pene}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . Quod videtur per illud Mt xviii: Serue nequam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 (Mt 18,32-34) \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 quia illud est contemptus prestiti beneficii non tantum, ita quod faciat equiualenciam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . \endash  (3\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[3].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 Utrum uirtus clavium extendat se ad remissionem culpe et pene}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . Quod non, nam dicit beatus Jeronimus super Matheum: In absoluendum peccatis idem operatur sacerdos electus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  (?) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 quam olim sacerdos legalis in leprosis mundandis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Sciendum quod quantum ad remissionem culpe diverse fuerunt oppiniones: Vna videtur fuisse Magistri in 4\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 o\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 , quod uirtus clauium in remissione culpe nihil operatur efficiendo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 sicut eciam supplicatio eius plus valeret\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 Petrus de Tarantasia, Comm. in IV Sent., lib. 4, dist. 18, q. 2, art. 1, quaestiuncula 1; Druck: Innocentii quinti pontificis maximi \u8230 \'85 in IV. librum sententiarum commentaria. Toulouse 1652. ND Ridgewood (New Jersey) 1964, Bd. 4, S. 209 (mit Abweichungen). Johannes Duns Scotus (Z. 11: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Jo Scoti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) als weitere Autorit\u228 \'e4t genannt, mit Anlehnungen an: Ordinatio, lib. 4, dist. 18; vgl. Duns Scotus, Op. om. (Vat.) 13, S. 228.}

