\pard\keep\keepn\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -262\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Johannes de Tambaco}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 De consolatione theologiae}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 I\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -II\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer. \endash  (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Prolog 1: \u8250 \'9bPrologus\u8249 \'8b \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Incipit prologus in librum de consolacione Theologie fratris Johannis de Tambaco ordinis predicatorum prouincie Theutonie sacre Theologie professoris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[3].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Quecumque scripta sunt (Rm 15,4). Quoniam autem secundum hoc ipse apostolus nobis insinuat}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 , doctrinam scriptam specialiter ad hoc tendere, ut per consolacionem scripturarum spem habeamus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85; (3\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Prolog 2: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Item prologus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Incipit cum quadam adhuc prefacione liber de consolacione theologie primus continens consolacionum remedia opportuna contra illa turbatiua, que opponuntur mundane felicitati et prosperitati\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Cum humanum genus post lapsum primorum parentium de paradiso voluptatis eiectum}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85; (4\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 1: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Capitulum primum continens consolaciones super carencia mundane felicitatis et super infelicitate et miseriis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Primo itaque principaliter quatuor tristibus predicte domine appropinquantibus}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  et astantibus coram\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85; (24\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 2; (49\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 3; (72\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 4; (97\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 5; (104\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 6; (109\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 7; (127\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 8; (145\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 9; (161\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 10; (175\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 11; (196\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 12; (210\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 13; (241\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 14; (254\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 15, (262\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) expl.: \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quibus communicatur eius imperium cum omnipotencia honoreque et gloria eius tam sublimis quam nobis prestare dignetur ipse Christus in secula seculorum benedictus. Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 1422\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Per manus fratris Jo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [annes] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Wissenhorn\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b. \endash  Kolophon: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Explicit liber de consolacione theologie per fratrem Johannem de Tambaco ordinis predicatorum prouincie theutonie sacre theologie professorem Anno verbi incarnati 1422 ipsa die Medardi Episcopi et Confessoris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (8. Juni 1422). Im Fu\u223 \'dfsteg von derselben Hand: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Jo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [annes] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Yrsinger\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (263\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -266\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Kapitelverzeichnis: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Hic ponuntur loco tabule libri parciales et capitula tocius libri de consolacione theologie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  Kolophon: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5686/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Explicit hoc totum per manus fratris Johannis Yrrsinger professus in Cesarea scriptum in Mulenbrunnense Anno etc die Procto}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Protho oder Proclo?). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Deo gracias\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  Dar\u252 \'fcber von anderer Hand: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Dator istius libri est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (dar\u252 \'fcber: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 fuit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 dominus Tristramus de Nusperg, Canonicus et custos ecclesie Fris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 [ingensis] 1477. \endash  267\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -III\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 Druck: GW M14759 = BSB-Ink I-524. \endash  Teildruck: Johannes von Dambach, De consolatione theologiae. Libri I-III. (Editio critica), hrsg. von Piotr \plain \f2\scaps\lang1024\fs20 Smoli\plain \f2\scaps\lang1024\fs20 \u324 \'f1\plain \f2\scaps\lang1024\fs20 ski\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Lublin 2009 (Acta mediaevalia 21), S. XIV/XXXVIII (Hs. genannt, Sigle M\plain \f1\sub\lang1033\fs20 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ), LIV (Stemma codicum), 3-214 (Edition). \endash  Albert \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Auer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Johannes von Dambach und die Trostb\u252 \'fccher vom 11. bis zum 16. Jahrhundert. M\u252 \'fcnster 1928 (BGPhMA 27,1-2), S. 7f. (Hs. genannt), 16-18 (zur Datierung), 77f., 86, 96. \endash  Vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Stegm\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 ller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , RB 9348. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Kaeppeli\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Scriptores Nr. 2256. \endash  Vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Bloomfield\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Incipits Nr. 5015. \endash  Franz Josef \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Worstbrock\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , in: \u178 \'b2VL 4 (1983), Sp. 571-577. \endash  Carmen \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Cardelle de Hartmann\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Lateinische Dialoge 1200-1400. Literaturhistorische Studie und Repertorium. Leiden/Boston 2007 (Mittellateinische Studien und Texte 37), R61, S. 197f., 614-624, hier S. 620 (Hs. genannt).}

