\pard\keep\keepn\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -46\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Pseudo-Marcus Tullius Cicero}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Rhetorica ad Herennium, cum glossis}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Lib. 1: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Marcii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Tulii Ciceronis ad Herennium Rethoricorum liber primus incipit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Etsi}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17  [in] {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 negotiis familiaribus impediti uix satis otium studio suppeditare possumus}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85; (6\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 2; (17\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 3; (26\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) lib. 4, expl.: \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 si rationes preceptionis diligentia consequemur exercitationis. Finis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Marci Tulii Ciceronis rethoricorum liber explicit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Beginn der Glossen von der Hand des Johannes Heller: \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Orator differt a rethore et sophista. Orator est ille, qui non solum sit autor, sed eciam exercet ut Cicero in oracionibus. Sophista est medium inter rethorem et oratorem. Rhetor dicit de arte, orator exercet artem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Ocium. Genera ocii quatuor sunt: Primum est, quod a uulgaribus dicitur. Secundum est, cum sumus aliqualiter in studio defessi, tunc vacamus circa ocium causa recreandi animum. Terciomodo ocium vocamus, quando patimur uel infirmi sumus, vnde dicimus, quare ociamini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (?). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quartomodo ocium dicitur, quando operam damus studio, quia quo ad corpus in ocio stamus, quo ad animum minime et de hoc intendit Cicero\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Druck: Incerti auctoris de ratione dicendi ad C. Herennium libri IV. M. Tulli Ciceronis ad Herennium libri VI. Rhetorica ad Herennium, ed. Friedrich \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Marx\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Leipzig 1894.}

