\pard\keep\keepn\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -353\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Hugutio}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Magnae derivationes}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rab\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Prolog: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Cvm nostri prothoplasti suggestiua prevaricacione humanum genus}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  a sue dignitatis culmine quam a longe deciderit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash  1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer. \endash  (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -353\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Glossar: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Augeo, -es, -xi, -ctum. Amplificare uel augmentum dare}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  et inde hic auctor id est augmentator\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ...\endash ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Zorobabel id est iste magister de Babilonia. In Babilone enim ortus est vbi et princeps gentis Iudee exstit. Zoroastrum viuum sydus. Zographia pictor\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (308\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Z. 40) Text springt von \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 venitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 etiam diserto -as \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (Druck: S. 1087 [58]) auf ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 in seui et supinum in situm uel in satum, neutra sunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Druck: S. 1088 [73]). Die Textl\u252 \'fccke als Nachtrag auf 307b\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  mit Leseanweisung am Rand von Dytelsteters Hand: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Quere hoc signum in folio sequenti in fine tercie line\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 per vnum s id est disertum facere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 quod faciunt preteritum in seui et supinum in situm uel in satum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Druck: S. 1087 [58]-1088 [73]). \endash  (353\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2]/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Kolophon}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Finitum est opus hoc per manus Johannis Dystelstetis anno domini Millesimo Quadringentesimo Nono feria quarta post festum sancti Egidii etc\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . (5. September 1409). \endash  353\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 -354\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Druck\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 : \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Uguccione da Pisa, Derivationes. Edizione critica princeps a cura di Enzo \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Cecchini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Bde. 1-2. Florenz 2004 (Edizione nazionale dei testi mediolatini 11 = Serie I,6,1) (ohne diese Hs.). \endash  Claus \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Riessner\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Die \u8222 \'84Magnae derivationes\ldblquote  des Uguccione da Pisa und ihre Bedeutung f\u252 \'fcr die romanische Philologie. Rom 1965 (Temi e testi 11), S. 194-233. \endash  Zur hsl. \u220 \'dcberlieferung vgl. Aristide \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Marigo,\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 I codici manoscritti delle \u8222 \'84Derivationes\ldblquote  di Uguccione Pisano. Saggio d\rquote inventario bibliografico con appendice sui codici del \u8222 \'84catholicon\ldblquote  di Giovanni da Genova. Rom 1936, S. 25 (Hs. genannt). \endash  Lit.: Klaus \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Grubm\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 ller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Vocabularius Ex quo. M\u252 \'fcnchen 1967 (MTU 17), S. 14, 21-26. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Bursill-Hall\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Census, S. 148 Nr. 62 (Hs. genannt). \endash  Ruth \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Weigand\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Huguccio (Uguccio, Hugo, Hugutio), in: LexMA 5 (1991), Sp. 181f. \endash  Wolfgang P. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 M\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 ller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Huguccio, The life, works, and thought of a twelfth-century jurist. Washington 1994 (Studies in medieval and early modern canon law 3), S. 43-48, 64-66. \endash  Le \u8222 \'84Derivazioni\ldblquote  di Uguccione da Pisa. Atti dell\rquote incontro di studi all\rquote Universit\u224 \'e0 di Zurigo 10 febbraio 2006, in: Archivum latinitatis medii aevi 64 (2006), S. 241-275 (Kolloquium anl\u228 \'e4\u223 \'dflich der 2004 erschienenen kritischen Edition mit Beitr\u228 \'e4gen von Claudio \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Leonardi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Darko \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Senekovic\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Michele \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Loporcaro\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Peter \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Stotz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Michelangelo \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Picone\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ).}

