\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Hic incipit liber seu tractatus de mistica theologia magistri Johannis Gersonis doctoris sacre Theologie cancellarii parisiensis per modum consideracionum continens duas partes etc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 \u8249 \'8b, (204\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Prolog: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Astrinxit me promissio nouissima illud aggredi}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85, pars prima: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Aliqua est theologia mistica}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 (221\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) pars 2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 a\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Tractantes in lectionibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8230 \'85\endash \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 dilectus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [meus] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 mihi, et ego illi etc. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 (233\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 Expliciunt consideraciones tractactus siue libelli de mistica theologia venerabilis Johannis Gerson olim cancellarii ecclesie parysiensis, edita ab eodem anno domini millesimo quadringentesimoseptimo, et recensite ab eo siue relecte et probate sicut propria manu subscripsit in exemplari, quod ad carthusiam misit de ciuitate Lugdunensi Anno domini 1422\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Ed.: Ioannis Carlerii de Gerson de mystica theologia, hrsg. von Andr\u233 \'e9 \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Combes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 . Lugano 1958, S. 1-217, zur Hs. S. XV (Sigle o, Fassung C/C\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ); das Explicit ist in 10 Hss. belegt (ebd. S. XIX), die vor allem aus oberbayerischen Kl\u246 \'f6stern stammen (Tegernsee, Andechs, Diessen, Indersdorf, Steingaden).  }

